comments.message:
Do you have a need for modeling the switch or only the Ports? 
/redfish/v1/Systems/{ComputerSystemId}/FabricAdapters/{FabricAdapterId}/Ports/{PortId}
might be another choice..

We might add properties for the Switch in the future.

One of the devices that gets enabled with this patch is an NIC that has an integrated PCIe Switch. It has PCIe ports as well as Network ports. See dbus-sensors patch - https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/83202 

@ed@tanous.net suggested that such a device is not exactly a Fabric Adapter and the FabricAdapter URI cannot be used for such a device, and hence the Switch URI is used.

Should this check NotFound case like?

```
        if (ec.value() == boost::system::errc::io_error || ec.value() == EBADR)
        {
            // Not found
            messages::resourceNotFound(asyncResp->res, "Switch", switchId);
            return;
        }
```

Should this be done by using `collection_util::getCollectionMembers()` like this, and remove the above `handleFabricSwitchPathsSwitchCollection()`?


```
   std::string switchUrl = boost::urls::format("/redfish/v1/Fabrics/{}/Switches", fabricId);

    asyncResp->res.jsonValue["@odata.id"] = switchUrl;
    asyncResp->res.jsonValue["@odata.type"] =
        "#SwitchCollection.SwitchCollection";
    asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Name"] = fabricId + " Switch Collection";

    collection_util::getCollectionMembers(
        asyncResp, boost::urls::url(switchUrl), switchInterfaces,
        "/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory");
```
